{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789292171,"nonce":"uGHXnggPIap8Z5qi3u0A4d/m3WE=","message":"a523117, 2b4fbe2, 7dfd513: field-kind invariants. Every class keeps a byte per instance field (ObjClass::field_kinds, at CLASS_FIELD_KINDS for compiled code), or'd by every store (interpreter, helpers, Cranelift baseline when the LLVM tier is on, LLVM code for values not known to be Nums) and preset to 'other' for a field a constructor does not assign in its entry block before this escapes. A guarded getter whose byte is exactly 'num' checks the byte instead of the loaded value; the byte is read through an external global mapped to the array (add_global_mapping) so LLVM can hoist the checks into loop preheaders — a bare inttoptr constant is not dereferenceable and LICM would not move it. Subscripts and list-protocol calls in a speculating body get a SlowPathExit (resume at the instruction), so nbody's loops contain no calls and the field loads are plain double loads. Also found and fixed on the way (d4532dc): the Cranelift inner f64 body of a Num-guarded recursive function passed raw f64 parameters to other calls, so bottomUpTree never compiled; ash/binary_trees off 6.3 s -\u003e 2.5 s.\n\nNUC: bench/ash/nbody 1.54 s -\u003e 1.20 s (off 7.2 s; Ash AOT 0.72 s); ash/binary_trees 2.5 s either tier (allocation-bound); mandelbrot 0.46; method_call/closure_call 0.11/0.10; delta_blue 0.14 (off 0.11). Mac nbody 1.21 s (Ash hybrid 0.53 s).\n\nSeen once and not reproduced since: an LLVM compile of a binary_trees body failed with an OSR live-in that had no slot (now a compile error instead of a panic on the promoter thread). What remains in nbody's loop: the class-hit flag test and fields-pointer reload per receiver, the i64-\u003edouble moves where a value is also held boxed for a deopt state, and the outer loop's list subscript checks.","files":null}]}